window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["crewai"]=[{"id":"crewai-f0001","card":"q-crewai-001-1-core-concepts","sec":"crewai-s002","q":"What are the four CrewAI building blocks?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Building block</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Crew</strong></td><td>Top-level orchestrator. Holds agents and tasks, picks execution order, starts the run, collects the result (acts like a project manager).</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Agent</strong></td><td>Autonomous, LLM-powered team member with a role. The only autonomous component.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Task</strong></td><td>Actionable step that breaks down the crew's goal.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Process</strong></td><td>Workflow management: how tasks are assigned and in what order. <code>sequential</code> or <code>hierarchical</code>.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0002","card":"q-crewai-001-1-core-concepts","sec":"crewai-s002","q":"What is a CrewAI crew?","a":"<p>The top-level orchestrator. It holds agents and tasks, picks the execution order, starts the run and collects the result. It acts like a project manager.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0003","card":"q-crewai-001-1-core-concepts","sec":"crewai-s002","q":"Which CrewAI component is the only autonomous one?","a":"<p>The agent. It is an LLM-powered team member with a role. It uses tools, can delegate and receive tasks, and makes its own decisions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0004","card":"q-crewai-001-1-core-concepts","sec":"crewai-s002","q":"What does a good CrewAI task need?","a":"<p>A clear objective, optional tools, and output that can be handed to the next agent. Good task breakdown is critical to success.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0005","card":"q-crewai-001-1-core-concepts","sec":"crewai-s002","q":"Which supplementary components does CrewAI have?","a":"<p><strong>Tools</strong> (external actions), <strong>Memory</strong> (retain information across tasks) and <strong>Knowledge</strong> (domain-specific information).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0006","card":"q-crewai-001-1-core-concepts","sec":"crewai-s002","q":"What is the success formula for a CrewAI project?","a":"<p>Accurately defined agents plus well-described tasks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0007","card":"q-crewai-001-1-core-concepts","sec":"crewai-s002","q":"How might an article crew be broken into tasks?","a":"<p>Research, analyze, outline and write tasks. An email task would use an email agent with email tools.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0008","card":"q-crewai-002-2-setup-and-project-types","sec":"crewai-s003","q":"What are the requirements for installing CrewAI?","a":"<p>Python 3.10 or newer and up to 3.13. <code>uv</code> is the preferred package manager over pip.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0009","card":"q-crewai-002-2-setup-and-project-types","sec":"crewai-s003","q":"How do you install <code>uv</code> on macOS or Linux, and on Windows?","a":"<p>macOS/Linux:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh</code></pre></div>\n<p>Windows PowerShell:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c &quot;irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 | iex&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0010","card":"q-crewai-002-2-setup-and-project-types","sec":"crewai-s003","q":"How do you install, confirm and upgrade the CrewAI CLI with <code>uv</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>uv tool install crewai\nuv tool list                          # confirm\nuv tool install crewai --upgrade      # upgrade</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0011","card":"q-crewai-002-2-setup-and-project-types","sec":"crewai-s003","q":"What do you do if <code>crewai install</code> fails with <code>psycopg2-binary</code> errors?","a":"<p>PostgreSQL (or its tools) is missing from the system, or its paths are not global. Install it:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>brew install postgresql                                   # macOS\nsudo apt-get install postgresql postgresql-contrib        # Ubuntu/Debian</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0012","card":"q-crewai-003-from-scratch-vs-scaffolded","sec":"crewai-s004","q":"CrewAI from-scratch vs scaffolded project?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>From scratch</th><th>Scaffolded (CLI)</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Setup</td><td><code>mkdir</code> + venv + <code>pip install crewai</code></td><td><code>crewai create crew &lt;name&gt;</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Structure</td><td>You define it</td><td>Standard boilerplate</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Agent/task config</td><td>Python code</td><td>YAML (<code>agents.yaml</code>, <code>tasks.yaml</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Install deps</td><td><code>pip install crewai</code></td><td><code>crewai install</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Learning, demos</td><td>Production</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0013","card":"q-crewai-003-from-scratch-vs-scaffolded","sec":"crewai-s004","q":"What is the recommended learning path for CrewAI project types?","a":"<p>Learn from scratch, then translate to scaffolded for production.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0014","card":"q-crewai-003-from-scratch-vs-scaffolded","sec":"crewai-s004","q":"What are the commands to set up a CrewAI project from scratch?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>mkdir my_first_crew\ncd my_first_crew\npython -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate          # Windows: .venv\\Scripts\\activate\npip install crewai</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0015","card":"q-crewai-003-from-scratch-vs-scaffolded","sec":"crewai-s004","q":"How do you create and install a scaffolded CrewAI project?","a":"<p>Create it with the CLI, then run <code>crewai install</code> at the project root. It creates the venv and installs dependencies. The create step prompts for LLM provider, model and API key (you can skip the key).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>crewai create crew sample_scaffolded_project   # prompts: LLM provider, model, API key (can skip)\ncrewai install                                 # run at project root; creates venv and installs deps</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0016","card":"q-crewai-003-from-scratch-vs-scaffolded","sec":"crewai-s004","q":"What is the structure of a scaffolded CrewAI project?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>knowledge/</code>: CSV, PDF, Excel for RAG over private data.</li>\n  <li><code>src/&lt;project&gt;/config/agents.yaml</code>: agent definitions.</li>\n  <li><code>src/&lt;project&gt;/config/tasks.yaml</code>: task definitions.</li>\n  <li><code>src/&lt;project&gt;/tools/</code>: custom tools.</li>\n  <li><code>crew.py</code>: crew, agents and tasks are defined here.</li>\n  <li><code>main.py</code>: entry point for run, train, replay, test.</li>\n  <li><code>tests/</code>, <code>.env</code> (model provider and API keys) and <code>pyproject.toml</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0017","card":"q-crewai-003-from-scratch-vs-scaffolded","sec":"crewai-s004","q":"What does the <code>.env</code> file of a CrewAI project hold?","a":"<p>The model and the provider key, using the provider's standard variable name:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">.env</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>MODEL=gpt-4o\nOPENAI_API_KEY=&lt;your-api-key&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0018","card":"q-crewai-004-3-api-keys","sec":"crewai-s005","q":"OpenAI vs Google vs Anthropic API keys in the CrewAI course?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>OpenAI</th><th>Google Generative AI</th><th>Anthropic</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>URL</td><td>platform.openai.com</td><td>aistudio.google.com</td><td>console.anthropic.com</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Free tier</td><td>No, credits must be purchased first</td><td>Yes</td><td>Limited free plan</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Key viewable later</td><td>No, shown once</td><td>Yes, always</td><td>No, shown once</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Needs cloud project</td><td>No</td><td>Yes, a GCP project</td><td>No</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Grouping</td><td>Projects</td><td>GCP projects</td><td>Workspaces</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Per-key permissions</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0019","card":"q-crewai-004-3-api-keys","sec":"crewai-s005","q":"In the CrewAI course, how do you create an OpenAI API key?","a":"<p>Go to Settings &gt; API keys &gt; Create new secret key. Add a payment method and credits under Billing. Copy the key immediately because it is shown once.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0020","card":"q-crewai-004-3-api-keys","sec":"crewai-s005","q":"In the CrewAI course, how do you create a Google Generative AI API key?","a":"<p>Create a GCP project first. Then in AI Studio choose Get API Key &gt; Create API key in existing project.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0021","card":"q-crewai-004-3-api-keys","sec":"crewai-s005","q":"In the CrewAI course, how do you create an Anthropic API key?","a":"<p>Go to Settings &gt; API keys &gt; Create key, and choose the workspace and a name. Copy the key immediately because it is shown once.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0022","card":"q-crewai-004-3-api-keys","sec":"crewai-s005","q":"In the CrewAI course, which environment variable names hold the OpenAI, Google and Anthropic keys?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">.env</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxx\nGOOGLE_API_KEY=AIzaXxxxxxxx\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxx</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0023","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"In the CrewAI YouTube ideas crew, how is the idea generator agent defined?","a":"<p>Its role is a generator of creative ideas for YouTube. Its goal is a diverse and extensive list of video ideas without any initial judgment:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>idea_generator_agent = Agent(\n    role=&quot;Generator of creative ideas for YouTube&quot;,\n    goal=&quot;Generate a diverse and extensive list of ideas for YouTube videos &quot;\n         &quot;without any initial judgment.&quot;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0024","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"In the CrewAI YouTube ideas crew, how is the idea filter agent defined?","a":"<p>Its role is the analytical evaluator of the brainstormed ideas. Its goal is to select the most promising and actionable ideas against criteria relevant to YouTube:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>idea_filter_agent = Agent(\n    goal=&quot;Select the most promising and actionable video ideas from the list &quot;\n         &quot;based on predefined criteria relevant to YouTube.&quot;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0025","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"What does the first CrewAI crew (YouTube ideas) consist of?","a":"<p>Two agents (idea generator and idea filter), two tasks and a sequential process. Task 1 output feeds Task 2.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0026","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"Which LLM does a CrewAI crew use by default, and what must you set first?","a":"<p>The default LLM is OpenAI GPT-4, so set the key first:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxx\npython youtube_crew.py</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0027","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"Which four classes do you import for a basic CrewAI script?","a":"<p><code>Agent</code>, <code>Task</code>, <code>Crew</code> and <code>Process</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from crewai import Agent, Task, Crew, Process</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0028","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"How do you define a task with a dynamic topic in CrewAI?","a":"<p>Put a <code>{topic}</code> placeholder in the description and set an expected output:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>idea_generation_task = Task(\n    description=&quot;Brainstorm ideas for YouTube videos on the topic: {topic}&quot;,\n    expected_output=&quot;A bullet list of ideas. Example:\\n- Idea 1\\n- Idea 2&quot;,\n    agent=idea_generator_agent\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0029","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"How do you assemble and run the YouTube ideas crew?","a":"<p>Create the <code>Crew</code> with a sequential process and call <code>kickoff</code> with inputs:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>idea_generation_crew = Crew(\n    agents=[idea_generator_agent, idea_filter_agent],\n    tasks=[idea_generation_task, idea_filtering_task],\n    process=Process.sequential,\n    verbose=True\n)\n\nidea_generation_crew.kickoff(inputs={&quot;topic&quot;: &quot;Foundational Models&quot;})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0030","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"What does <code>kickoff(inputs={...})</code> do with <code>{topic}</code>?","a":"<p>It fills the dynamic variable, which makes tasks reusable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0031","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"What does <code>verbose=True</code> do on a crew?","a":"<p>It shows each agent's reasoning.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0032","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"What does the YouTube ideas crew output?","a":"<p>3-5 filtered ideas, each with reasoning.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0033","card":"q-crewai-005-4-first-crew-youtube-ideas","sec":"crewai-s006","q":"In the CrewAI YouTube crew, what expected output does the idea filtering task ask for?","a":"<p>Top 3-5 ideas with reasoning, in this format:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>expected_output=&quot;Top 3-5 ideas with reasoning. Format:\\n&quot;\n                &quot;- Idea: &lt;idea&gt;\\n  Reasoning: &lt;why selected&gt;&quot;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0034","card":"q-crewai-006-5-agents","sec":"crewai-s007","q":"What is a CrewAI agent and what design principle applies?","a":"<p>A single autonomous unit built for one specific problem. The principle is <strong>one agent = one focused responsibility</strong>, for example Tax Auditor vs Tax Filer, or Deal Finder vs Inventory vs Delivery agent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0035","card":"q-crewai-006-5-agents","sec":"crewai-s007","q":"What can a CrewAI agent do?","a":"<p>Perform a specific task, make decisions guided by <code>role</code> and <code>goal</code>, use tools, collaborate with other agents, and use memory of past communications.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0036","card":"q-crewai-006-5-agents","sec":"crewai-s007","q":"What is the agent's role within a crew, and can each agent have its own LLM?","a":"<p>Agents are the action takers and the only autonomous component, powered by an LLM. Each agent can be given a different LLM.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0037","card":"q-crewai-007-three-required-attributes","sec":"crewai-s008","q":"Which three attributes does every CrewAI agent require?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>role</code></td><td>Who the agent is: function and expertise</td><td>Senior Researcher, Marketing Expert</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>goal</code></td><td>Individual objective that guides decisions</td><td>\"Gather a set of reviews of electronic products that represent a range of opinions\"</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>backstory</code></td><td>Persona, experience, extra context beyond the role</td><td>\"A professional traveler with a knack for finding interesting places...\"</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0038","card":"q-crewai-007-three-required-attributes","sec":"crewai-s008","q":"In CrewAI, what does an agent's <code>goal</code> do?","a":"<p>It is the individual objective that guides the agent's decisions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0039","card":"q-crewai-007-three-required-attributes","sec":"crewai-s008","q":"In CrewAI, what does an agent's <code>backstory</code> add?","a":"<p>The persona, experience and extra context beyond the role.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0040","card":"q-crewai-008-two-ways-to-define-agents","sec":"crewai-s009","q":"Direct code vs YAML config for defining CrewAI agents?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Direct code</th><th>YAML config</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Where</td><td><code>.py</code> file</td><td><code>config/agents.yaml</code> + <code>crew.py</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Creation</td><td><code>Agent(role=..., goal=..., backstory=...)</code></td><td><code>Agent(config=...)</code> + <code>@agent</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Project type</td><td>From scratch</td><td>Scaffolded</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Trade-off</td><td>Simpler to learn; config mixed with code</td><td>Config separated from code; cleaner with many agents</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0041","card":"q-crewai-008-two-ways-to-define-agents","sec":"crewai-s009","q":"In CrewAI, how do you define an agent in direct code?","a":"<p>Import <code>Agent</code> and pass <code>role</code>, <code>goal</code> and <code>backstory</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from crewai import Agent\n\ndestination_researcher = Agent(\n    role=&quot;An explorer and information gatherer responsible for finding &quot;\n         &quot;interesting places and activities related to the travel request.&quot;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0042","card":"q-crewai-008-two-ways-to-define-agents","sec":"crewai-s009","q":"Which two agents does the direct-code travel crew define?","a":"<p>A researcher (<code>destination_researcher</code>) and an itinerary planner (<code>itinerary_planner</code>). The planner organizes the gathered information into a logical and simple one day plan.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0043","card":"q-crewai-009-two-ways-to-define-agents","sec":"crewai-s009","q":"How is an agent laid out in <code>config/agents.yaml</code>?","a":"<p>The agent name is a top-level key, with <code>role</code>, <code>goal</code> and <code>backstory</code> beneath it:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>destination_researcher:\n  role: &gt;\n    An explorer and information gatherer responsible for finding\n    interesting places and activities related to the travel request.</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0044","card":"q-crewai-009-two-ways-to-define-agents","sec":"crewai-s009","q":"How does <code>crew.py</code> load an agent from YAML?","a":"<p><code>@agent</code> (from <code>crewai.project</code>) marks an agent factory, and <code>config=</code> pulls role, goal and backstory for that key:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from crewai.project import agent\n\nclass MyCrew:\n    agents_config = &quot;config/agents.yaml&quot;\n\n    @agent\n    def destination_researcher(self) -&gt; Agent:\n        return Agent(\n            config=self.agents_config[&quot;destination_researcher&quot;]\n        )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0045","card":"q-crewai-009-two-ways-to-define-agents","sec":"crewai-s009","q":"In CrewAI, what name must match when defining agents with YAML?","a":"<p>The method name must match the YAML key.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0046","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"Which agent parameters are required in CrewAI?","a":"<p>Only <code>role</code>, <code>goal</code> and <code>backstory</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0047","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"What does the agent <code>llm</code> parameter do?","a":"<p>It sets the LLM to use. The default is OpenAI GPT-4. It needs the provider's key in <code>.env</code> or the environment.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0048","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"In CrewAI, which agent parameters belong to memory and context?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>memory</code>: conversation history, default <code>False</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>respect_context_window</code>: keep prompts and responses within the LLM context window.</li>\n  <li><code>knowledge_sources</code>: external knowledge (websites, files).</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0049","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"What do the execution control parameters do on a CrewAI agent?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>max_iter</code></td><td>Max LLM requests before timeout/fallback (prevents infinite loops)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>max_execution_time</code></td><td>Per-request timeout in seconds (avoids hangs)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>max_rpm</code></td><td>Max requests per minute (avoids rate-limit errors)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>max_retry_limit</code></td><td>Retries after an error (self-heal transient failures)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0050","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"How does code execution work for a CrewAI agent?","a":"<p><code>allow_code_execution</code> defaults to <code>False</code>. <code>code_execution_mode=\"safe\"</code> runs in Docker (production). <code>\"unsafe\"</code> runs directly and is for trusted environments only.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0051","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"In CrewAI, what are the template parameters of an agent?","a":"<p><code>system_template</code>, <code>prompt_template</code> and <code>response_template</code>. They control the structure of system instructions, request prompts and model responses.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0052","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"What do <code>function_calling_llm</code>, <code>allow_delegation</code>, <code>cache</code> and <code>embedder</code> do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>function_calling_llm</code>: a separate LLM just for tool calling.</li>\n  <li><code>allow_delegation</code>: lets the agent hand tasks to other agents.</li>\n  <li><code>cache</code>: caches tool usage, default <code>True</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>embedder</code>: embedder config used by the agent.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0053","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"In CrewAI, how do you set execution control parameters on an agent?","a":"<p>Pass them to <code>Agent</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>max_iter=15,\nmax_execution_time=300,\nmax_rpm=10,\nmax_retry_limit=3,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0054","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"In CrewAI, how do you give an agent tools and a separate tool-calling LLM?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tools=[search_tool, scrape_tool],\nfunction_calling_llm=&quot;gpt-4o&quot;,\nallow_delegation=True,\ncache=True</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0055","card":"q-crewai-010-agent-parameter-groups","sec":"crewai-s010","q":"In CrewAI, how do you pick a Gemini model for an agent?","a":"<p>Set the <code>llm</code> parameter:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm=&quot;gemini/gemini-2.0-flash&quot;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0056","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"Why do CrewAI agents need tools?","a":"<p>Agents without tools are essentially smart chatbots. Tools (skills or functions for external actions) are what make an agent agentic.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0057","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"Which kinds of CrewAI tools exist?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Examples</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>CrewAI built-in</td><td><code>FileReadTool</code>, <code>GitHubSearchTool</code>, <code>SerperDevTool</code></td><td>Bundled in <code>crewai[tools]</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>LangChain tools</td><td><code>TavilySearchTool</code>, <code>TwilioTool</code></td><td>Web browsing, SMS</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Bridge tools</td><td><code>ComposioTool</code></td><td>250+ tools from Composio</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Custom</td><td>Extend <code>BaseTool</code></td><td>Turn Python classes into tools</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0058","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"Where do you import CrewAI tools from, and are they all free?","a":"<p>Import from <code>crewai_tools</code>, not <code>crewai</code>. Some tools are paid: DALL-E, Composio, and Serper beyond its free tier.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0059","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"What is <code>SerperDevTool</code> and what does it need?","a":"<p>A Google Search API tool with a free tier (key from serper.dev). It needs <code>SERPER_API_KEY</code>. It returns JSON (credits_used, results with title, link and snippet), which agents process automatically.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0060","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"How do you install CrewAI tools and set the Serper key?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install &#x27;crewai[tools]&#x27;\nexport SERPER_API_KEY=&lt;your_serper_api_key&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0061","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"How do you test a CrewAI tool before assigning it to an agent?","a":"<p>Call <code>.run()</code> directly:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(browse_tool.run(search_query=&quot;AI Agents&quot;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0062","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"In CrewAI, how do you assign several tools to an agent?","a":"<p><code>tools</code> takes a list:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tools=[browse_tool, file_tool]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0063","card":"q-crewai-011-6-tools","sec":"crewai-s011","q":"How do you write a custom CrewAI tool?","a":"<p>Extend <code>BaseTool</code> with a name, a description and a <code>_run</code> method:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from crewai.tools import BaseTool\n\nclass MyCustomTool(BaseTool):\n    name: str = &quot;My Tool&quot;\n    description: str = &quot;What this tool does&quot;\n\n    def _run(self, argument: str) -&gt; str:\n        # Custom logic here\n        return &quot;result&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0064","card":"q-crewai-012-7-memory","sec":"crewai-s012","q":"What does memory give CrewAI agents?","a":"<p>Agents reason better, learn from earlier interactions, keep context during a session, and improve with use (fine-tuning strategies from past errors). It goes beyond the LLM context window.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0065","card":"q-crewai-012-7-memory","sec":"crewai-s012","q":"What are the CrewAI memory types?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Stores</th><th>Mechanism</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Short-term</td><td>Recent interactions and outcomes</td><td>Temporary, uses RAG; gives context for the current task</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Long-term</td><td>Lessons and patterns from past runs</td><td>Persists insights, refines knowledge over time</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Entity</td><td>People, places, organizations</td><td>Deeper understanding and relationship mapping</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Contextual</td><td>Best composition of short-term, long-term and entity memory</td><td>Keeps coherence across a sequence of tasks</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>External</td><td>Outside providers</td><td>MemGPT, GraphRAG, Mem0</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0066","card":"q-crewai-012-7-memory","sec":"crewai-s012","q":"Which memory type benefits map to which benefit in CrewAI?","a":"<p>Contextual awareness comes from short-term plus contextual memory. Experience accumulation comes from long-term memory. Entity understanding comes from entity memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0067","card":"q-crewai-012-7-memory","sec":"crewai-s012","q":"Is CrewAI memory on by default, and how do you enable it?","a":"<p>No, <code>memory=False</code> by default. Enable it on an agent, or on the crew for all agents:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>crew = Crew(\n    agents=[agent1, agent2],\n    tasks=[task1, task2],\n    process=Process.sequential,\n    memory=True\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0068","card":"q-crewai-012-7-memory","sec":"crewai-s012","q":"Which embeddings does CrewAI memory use by default, and how do you change them?","a":"<p>The default embeddings are OpenAI's. Change them with <code>embedder</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>embedder={\n    &quot;provider&quot;: &quot;google&quot;,\n    &quot;config&quot;: {&quot;model&quot;: &quot;models/text-embedding-004&quot;}\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0069","card":"q-crewai-013-8-tasks","sec":"crewai-s013","q":"What is a CrewAI task?","a":"<p>The fundamental unit of work, a piece of the crew's overall goal. It encapsulates an objective, expected output, dependencies, needed data and context, and optional tools. Usually one task maps to one agent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0070","card":"q-crewai-014-execution-styles","sec":"crewai-s014","q":"In CrewAI, how do sequential and hierarchical task execution differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Sequential</th><th>Hierarchical</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Order</td><td>Linear, one after another</td><td>Branching and parallel</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Coordination</td><td>Output of one task feeds the next</td><td>Manager agent oversees and coordinates</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Fits</td><td>Step-by-step pipelines</td><td>Dynamic, multi-path workflows, decisions based on earlier outcomes</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0071","card":"q-crewai-015-core-parameters","sec":"crewai-s015","q":"What are the core parameters of a CrewAI task?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>Clear step toward the crew's goal. Supports <code>{variable}</code> placeholders.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>expected_output</code></td><td>What the result looks like. Including an example works as <strong>few-shot prompting</strong>.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>agent</code></td><td>Which agent performs it.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0072","card":"q-crewai-015-core-parameters","sec":"crewai-s015","q":"Why include an example in <code>expected_output</code>?","a":"<p>It works as <strong>few-shot prompting</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0073","card":"q-crewai-015-core-parameters","sec":"crewai-s015","q":"In CrewAI, which other task parameters exist besides description, expected_output and agent?","a":"<p><code>tools</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>human_input</code> (human-in-the-loop), <code>context</code>, <code>output_pydantic</code>, <code>output_json</code>, <code>output_file</code> and <code>async_execution</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0074","card":"q-crewai-016-direct-code-travel-crew","sec":"crewai-s016","q":"How do you write the research task of the travel crew in code?","a":"<p>Use a <code>{location}</code> dynamic variable, supplied at kickoff, and give an example output:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>travel_research_task = Task(\n    description=&quot;&quot;&quot;Use a web search tool to search for attractions, activities,\n    landmarks, or experiences relevant to {location}. Gather information about\n    popular spots, unique experiences, and practical details like general\n    location or type of activity. The focus is on identifying potential places\n    to include in a one-day plan.&quot;&quot;&quot;,\n    agent=destination_researcher\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0075","card":"q-crewai-016-direct-code-travel-crew","sec":"crewai-s016","q":"What does the itinerary planning task of the travel crew do with the first task's output?","a":"<p>The second task consumes the first task's output. It takes the list of potential options and structures them into a simple one-day itinerary.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0076","card":"q-crewai-016-direct-code-travel-crew","sec":"crewai-s016","q":"In the CrewAI travel crew, what example output does the research task give for Paris?","a":"<p>A list of places such as:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- Eiffel Tower — Iconic landmark\n- Louvre Museum — World-famous art museum</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0077","card":"q-crewai-016-direct-code-travel-crew","sec":"crewai-s016","q":"In the CrewAI travel crew, what does the itinerary task's expected output look like for Paris?","a":"<p>A chronological list with morning, late morning and afternoon entries:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- Morning: Visit the Eiffel Tower\n- Late Morning/Early Afternoon: Explore the Louvre Museum</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0078","card":"q-crewai-017-yaml-method","sec":"crewai-s017","q":"How do you define tasks in <code>config/tasks.yaml</code>?","a":"<p>The task name is the top-level key. <code>{location}</code> works the same way as in code:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>itinerary_planning_task:\n  description: &gt;\n    Take the list of potential options from the preceding task and structure\n    them into a simple one-day itinerary.\n  expected_output: &gt;\n    A simple sequenced one-day itinerary with activities in chronological order.\n  agent: itinerary_planner</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0079","card":"q-crewai-017-yaml-method","sec":"crewai-s017","q":"How does <code>crew.py</code> load a task from YAML?","a":"<p>Use <code>@task</code> from <code>crewai.project</code> and pull the config by key:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from crewai.project import task\n\nclass MyCrew:\n    tasks_config = &quot;config/tasks.yaml&quot;\n\n    @task\n    def travel_research_task(self) -&gt; Task:\n        return Task(\n            config=self.tasks_config[&quot;travel_research_task&quot;]\n        )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0080","card":"q-crewai-017-yaml-method","sec":"crewai-s017","q":"In CrewAI, which names must match when defining tasks in YAML?","a":"<p>The function name must match the task key in <code>tasks.yaml</code>. The <code>agent:</code> value must match a key in <code>agents.yaml</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0081","card":"q-crewai-018-managing-task-output","sec":"crewai-s018","q":"What is the default output of a CrewAI task?","a":"<p>A raw string, passed automatically to dependent tasks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0082","card":"q-crewai-018-managing-task-output","sec":"crewai-s018","q":"<code>output_pydantic</code> vs <code>output_json</code> vs <code>output_file</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Takes</th><th>Returns</th><th>Use for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>output_pydantic</code></td><td>Pydantic model class</td><td>Pydantic instance</td><td>Structured data inside Python</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>output_json</code></td><td>Pydantic model class</td><td>dict (JSON)</td><td>External APIs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>output_file</code></td><td>File path (relative or absolute)</td><td>Written to disk</td><td>Documents, articles</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0083","card":"q-crewai-018-managing-task-output","sec":"crewai-s018","q":"What is the difference between <code>output_pydantic</code> and <code>output_json</code>?","a":"<p>They take the same model and differ only in return type: a Pydantic instance vs a dict.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0084","card":"q-crewai-018-managing-task-output","sec":"crewai-s018","q":"In CrewAI, how do you make a task return structured data?","a":"<p>Define a Pydantic model and pass it as <code>output_pydantic</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class ItineraryOutput(BaseModel):\n    morning: str\n    afternoon: str\n    evening: str</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>output_pydantic=ItineraryOutput      # or output_json=ItineraryOutput\n# or output_file=&quot;outputs/itinerary.md&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0085","card":"q-crewai-018-managing-task-output","sec":"crewai-s018","q":"What does <code>task.output</code> return and which attributes work?","a":"<p>After <code>crew.kickoff()</code>, it returns a <code>TaskOutput</code>. <code>.raw</code> is always available. <code>.pydantic</code> needs <code>output_pydantic</code>. <code>.json_dict</code> needs <code>output_json</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(itinerary_task.output.raw)\nplan = itinerary_task.output.pydantic\nprint(plan.morning)\ndata = itinerary_task.output.json_dict\nprint(data[&quot;morning&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0086","card":"q-crewai-019-task-level-tools","sec":"crewai-s019","q":"What happens when both a task and its agent have tools in CrewAI?","a":"<p>Task <code>tools</code> override agent <code>tools</code> for that task, which reduces non-determinism. If only the agent has tools, it uses its own. If only the task has tools, the task's are used.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0087","card":"q-crewai-019-task-level-tools","sec":"crewai-s019","q":"In CrewAI, when would you give tools to a task rather than an agent?","a":"<p>For example a search tool on a research task (ground it in web data) or a database query tool on a summary task.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0088","card":"q-crewai-019-task-level-tools","sec":"crewai-s019","q":"In CrewAI, how do you give a task its own tool?","a":"<p>Pass <code>tools</code> to <code>Task</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>travel_research_task = Task(\n    description=&quot;Search for attractions and activities in {location}.&quot;,\n    expected_output=&quot;A list of places with names and categories.&quot;,\n    agent=destination_researcher,\n    tools=[browse_tool]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0089","card":"q-crewai-020-context-dependencies-between-tasks","sec":"crewai-s020","q":"In CrewAI, what does a task receive in sequential mode by default?","a":"<p>Only the immediately preceding task's output flows forward.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0090","card":"q-crewai-020-context-dependencies-between-tasks","sec":"crewai-s020","q":"What does the task <code>context</code> parameter do?","a":"<p>It takes a list of tasks and pulls output from several tasks or from a non-adjacent one.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0091","card":"q-crewai-020-context-dependencies-between-tasks","sec":"crewai-s020","q":"In CrewAI, how does a task depend on multiple tasks?","a":"<p>Pass both in <code>context</code>. Without it the task would only get the last task's output:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>comparison_task = Task(\n    description=&quot;Compare apples and oranges.&quot;,\n    expected_output=&quot;A comparison report.&quot;,\n    agent=analyst,\n    context=[apple_task, orange_task]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0092","card":"q-crewai-020-context-dependencies-between-tasks","sec":"crewai-s020","q":"In CrewAI, how does a task depend on a non-adjacent task?","a":"<p>Name only that task in <code>context</code>, for example skipping <code>task_c</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>context=[task_b]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0093","card":"q-crewai-021-async-execution","sec":"crewai-s021","q":"What does <code>async_execution=True</code> do on a task?","a":"<p>It runs the task in the background without blocking the main sequence.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0094","card":"q-crewai-021-async-execution","sec":"crewai-s021","q":"In CrewAI, when is async task execution useful?","a":"<p>For long-running work (scraping, summarizing millions of records) and non-critical work (logging, notifications, emailing).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0095","card":"q-crewai-021-async-execution","sec":"crewai-s021","q":"In CrewAI, how does a downstream task wait for an async task?","a":"<p>List the async task in <code>context</code>. The downstream task waits for it to finish:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>analysis_task = Task(\n    description=&quot;Analyze the scraped data.&quot;,\n    expected_output=&quot;Analysis report.&quot;,\n    agent=analyst_agent,\n    context=[scraping_task]      # waits for scraping_task\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0096","card":"q-crewai-021-async-execution","sec":"crewai-s021","q":"In CrewAI, how do async tasks behave in different scenarios?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Async task, nothing depends on it</td><td>Runs in background, blocks nothing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Async task + downstream <code>context</code></td><td>Downstream task waits for it</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Non-async tasks</td><td>Sequential as normal</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0097","card":"q-crewai-022-9-crews-and-process","sec":"crewai-s022","q":"What does a CrewAI crew do?","a":"<p>It is the central orchestrator. It defines the objective (through its tasks), supplies agents and tasks, determines order, runs execution and collects the final result.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0098","card":"q-crewai-022-9-crews-and-process","sec":"crewai-s022","q":"What are the main parameters of <code>Crew</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>agents</code></td><td>List of agents</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>tasks</code></td><td>List of tasks. For sequential, list order is execution order.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>process</code></td><td><code>Process.sequential</code> or <code>Process.hierarchical</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>verbose</code></td><td>Default <code>False</code>. Detailed logs. Recommended during development.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>memory</code></td><td>Default <code>False</code>. Shared memory across agents.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>manager_llm</code></td><td>LLM for the manager agent. Required for hierarchical only.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0099","card":"q-crewai-022-9-crews-and-process","sec":"crewai-s022","q":"<code>Process.sequential</code> vs <code>Process.hierarchical</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Process</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>Process.sequential</code></td><td>Tasks run one after another in list order. Output passes automatically. Best for linear workflows.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>Process.hierarchical</code></td><td>A manager agent (LLM) breaks the goal into subtasks and assigns them to agents autonomously. Supports branching and complex paths. Needs <code>manager_llm</code>.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0100","card":"q-crewai-022-9-crews-and-process","sec":"crewai-s022","q":"How do you build a sequential travel crew?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>traveling_crew = Crew(\n    agents=[destination_researcher, itinerary_planner],\n    tasks=[travel_research_task, itinerary_planning_task],\n    process=Process.sequential,\n    verbose=True,\n    memory=True       # optional\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0101","card":"q-crewai-022-9-crews-and-process","sec":"crewai-s022","q":"How do you build a hierarchical crew?","a":"<p>Use <code>Process.hierarchical</code> and set <code>manager_llm</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>hier_crew = Crew(\n    agents=[...],\n    tasks=[...],\n    process=Process.hierarchical,\n    manager_llm=&quot;gpt-4o&quot;,\n    verbose=True\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0102","card":"q-crewai-023-10-running-crews-and-reading-output","sec":"crewai-s023","q":"In the CrewAI travel crew, what does the sample itinerary output for Chicago look like?","a":"<p>A timed list of stops with walking or taxi times:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Morning:      Millennium Park — Cloud Gate sculpture\nLate Morning: Art Institute of Chicago (10-min walk)\nEarly Afternoon: Chicago River Walk (15-min walk)\nLate Evening: Navy Pier (10-min taxi) — waterfront, entertainment, dinner</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0103","card":"q-crewai-023-10-running-crews-and-reading-output","sec":"crewai-s023","q":"How do you run a CrewAI crew and fill its placeholders?","a":"<p>Set the provider key first (<code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>, <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>, <code>GOOGLE_API_KEY</code>). <code>kickoff(inputs={...})</code> triggers the run, and the keys map to <code>{placeholders}</code> in tasks.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxx\npython simple_travel_planning_crew.py</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0104","card":"q-crewai-023-10-running-crews-and-reading-output","sec":"crewai-s023","q":"What do you see with <code>verbose=True</code> during a run?","a":"<p>The ReAct loop (thought, action, observation) and a completion message.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0105","card":"q-crewai-023-10-running-crews-and-reading-output","sec":"crewai-s023","q":"What does <code>kickoff()</code> return and which attributes does it have?","a":"<p>A <code>CrewOutput</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>.raw</code></td><td>Raw string (always)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.pydantic</code></td><td>Pydantic model, if <code>output_pydantic</code> is set on the final task</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.json_dict</code></td><td>dict, if <code>output_json</code> is set on the final task</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.tasks_output</code></td><td>List of <code>TaskOutput</code>, one per task (same <code>.raw/.pydantic/.json_dict</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.token_usage</code></td><td>Token breakdown dict</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0106","card":"q-crewai-023-10-running-crews-and-reading-output","sec":"crewai-s023","q":"In CrewAI, how do you print the final output, per-task outputs and token usage?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>crew_output = traveling_crew.kickoff(inputs={&quot;location&quot;: &quot;Chicago&quot;})\n\nprint(f&quot;Final Output:\\n{crew_output.raw}&quot;)\nprint(f&quot;Tasks Output:\\n{crew_output.tasks_output}&quot;)\nprint(f&quot;Token Usage:\\n{crew_output.token_usage}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0107","card":"q-crewai-023-10-running-crews-and-reading-output","sec":"crewai-s023","q":"In CrewAI, how do you loop over every task's output?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for i, task_output in enumerate(crew_output.tasks_output):\n    print(f&quot;Task {i+1} Output:\\n{task_output.raw}\\n&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0108","card":"q-crewai-023-10-running-crews-and-reading-output","sec":"crewai-s023","q":"What does <code>token_usage</code> contain and why is it useful?","a":"<p>A token breakdown dict, useful for monitoring cost and optimizing LLM calls. It has <code>total_tokens</code>, <code>prompt_tokens</code>, <code>cached_tokens</code>, <code>completion_tokens</code> and <code>successful_requests</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n    &quot;total_tokens&quot;: 13812,\n    &quot;prompt_tokens&quot;: 13109,\n    &quot;cached_tokens&quot;: 3456,\n    &quot;completion_tokens&quot;: 703,\n    &quot;successful_requests&quot;: 7\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0109","card":"q-crewai-024-11-project-technical-writing-crew","sec":"crewai-s024","q":"What is the goal of the technical writing crew project?","a":"<p>Take any technical topic and produce a full Markdown article.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0110","card":"q-crewai-024-11-project-technical-writing-crew","sec":"crewai-s024","q":"What is the best practice for designing a crew?","a":"<p><strong>Start with the problem, not the agent.</strong> Break the problem into steps (topic, research, outline, write, edit, format), derive tasks, then derive agents.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0111","card":"q-crewai-024-11-project-technical-writing-crew","sec":"crewai-s024","q":"How is the technical writing crew configured?","a":"<p>It is a scaffolded project with YAML config, a sequential process and OpenAI GPT-4o. The final task writes a Markdown file via <code>output_file</code>. It needs two keys: <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> and <code>SERPER_API_KEY</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0112","card":"q-crewai-024-11-project-technical-writing-crew","sec":"crewai-s024","q":"How do you create and install the technical writing crew project?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>crewai create crew technical_writing_crew     # choose OpenAI, GPT-4o, enter key\ncd technical_writing_crew\ncrewai install\nexport SERPER_API_KEY=&lt;your_serper_api_key&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0113","card":"q-crewai-025-plan","sec":"crewai-s025","q":"What are the tasks, agents and dependencies of the technical writing crew?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Agent</th><th>Depends on (<code>context</code>)</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>research_task</code></td><td><code>technical_researcher</code> (SerperDevTool)</td><td>none</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>outline_task</code></td><td><code>article_strategist</code></td><td>research</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>writing_task</code></td><td><code>technical_writer</code></td><td>research, outline</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>editing_task</code></td><td><code>technical_editor</code></td><td>writing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>formatting_task</code></td><td><code>technical_editor</code></td><td>editing</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0114","card":"q-crewai-025-plan","sec":"crewai-s025","q":"Why does the technical writing crew have 5 tasks but 4 agents?","a":"<p>One agent can own several tasks. The editor edits and formats.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0115","card":"q-crewai-025-plan","sec":"crewai-s025","q":"Which agent has a tool in the technical writing crew, and why was a code interpreter skipped?","a":"<p>Only the researcher has a tool (web search). A code interpreter was skipped because it needs Docker and limits topics to Python.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0116","card":"q-crewai-026-agents-yaml","sec":"crewai-s026","q":"How are the technical writing crew's agents laid out in <code>agents.yaml</code>?","a":"<p>Each agent is a top-level key with <code>role</code>, <code>goal</code> and <code>backstory</code>. The four agents are <code>technical_researcher</code>, <code>article_strategist</code>, <code>technical_writer</code> and <code>technical_editor</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0117","card":"q-crewai-026-agents-yaml","sec":"crewai-s026","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, what is the technical researcher's goal?","a":"<p>To gather comprehensive and accurate details about the given technical research topic from reliable online places.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0118","card":"q-crewai-026-agents-yaml","sec":"crewai-s026","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, what are the goals of the article strategist, technical writer and technical editor?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Article strategist: define a logical and comprehensive outline based on the research findings.</li>\n  <li>Technical writer: write the actual prose, explaining complex concepts clearly and engagingly, including the necessary code samples based on the outline and research.</li>\n  <li>Technical editor: review the complete draft for technical accuracy, clarity, grammatical correctness and overall quality.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0119","card":"q-crewai-027-tasks-yaml","sec":"crewai-s027","q":"How are dependencies declared in the technical writing crew's <code>tasks.yaml</code>?","a":"<p>As explicit <code>context</code> lists, and <code>{topic}</code> is filled at kickoff:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>writing_task:\n  agent: technical_writer\n  context:\n    - research_task\n    - outline_task</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0120","card":"q-crewai-027-tasks-yaml","sec":"crewai-s027","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, what does the outline task do?","a":"<p>It analyzes the research notes and creates a logical, comprehensive article outline in Markdown. It marks where code samples or diagrams help using markers like \"code example needed\". Its <code>context</code> is <code>research_task</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0121","card":"q-crewai-027-tasks-yaml","sec":"crewai-s027","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, what do the editing and formatting tasks do and what context do they use?","a":"<p><code>editing_task</code> reviews the draft for technical accuracy, clarity, grammatical errors, typos, logical flow and consistency, with <code>context</code> <code>writing_task</code>. <code>formatting_task</code> makes the final content a clean, well-structured Markdown file, with <code>context</code> <code>editing_task</code>. Both use <code>technical_editor</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0122","card":"q-crewai-027-tasks-yaml","sec":"crewai-s027","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, what does the research task do?","a":"<p>It researches the topic <code>{topic}</code>, identifying key definitions, principles, use cases, best practices and challenges, using the web search tool. It then synthesizes the findings into structured research notes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0123","card":"q-crewai-027-tasks-yaml","sec":"crewai-s027","q":"Which settings live in YAML and which in <code>crew.py</code>?","a":"<p><code>description</code>, <code>expected_output</code>, <code>agent</code> and <code>context</code> live in YAML. Runtime-specific settings such as <code>output_file</code> live in <code>crew.py</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0124","card":"q-crewai-027-tasks-yaml","sec":"crewai-s027","q":"What name matching is required in the technical writing crew?","a":"<p><code>agent:</code> values in <code>tasks.yaml</code> must match <code>agents.yaml</code> keys. Method names in <code>crew.py</code> must match YAML keys.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0125","card":"q-crewai-028-crew-py-complete","sec":"crewai-s028","q":"How are agents configured in the technical writing <code>crew.py</code>?","a":"<p>Agents get <code>allow_delegation=False</code> (each must do its own task) and <code>verbose=True</code>. Only the researcher gets a tool.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@agent\ndef technical_researcher(self) -&gt; Agent:\n    web_search_tool = SerperDevTool()\n    return Agent(\n        config=self.agents_config[&quot;technical_researcher&quot;],\n        tools=[web_search_tool],\n        allow_delegation=False,\n        verbose=True\n    )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0126","card":"q-crewai-028-crew-py-complete","sec":"crewai-s028","q":"What are the class attributes of the <code>TechnicalWritingCrew</code> class?","a":"<p>Paths to the config files:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>agents_config = &quot;config/agents.yaml&quot;\ntasks_config = &quot;config/tasks.yaml&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0127","card":"q-crewai-028-crew-py-complete","sec":"crewai-s028","q":"How is a non-researcher agent defined in <code>crew.py</code>?","a":"<p>Same as the researcher but without a tool:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@agent\ndef article_strategist(self) -&gt; Agent:\n    return Agent(\n        config=self.agents_config[&quot;article_strategist&quot;],\n        allow_delegation=False,\n        verbose=True\n    )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0128","card":"q-crewai-029-crew-py-complete","sec":"crewai-s028","q":"How do <code>@task</code> methods load config in the technical writing crew?","a":"<p>Each returns a <code>Task</code> with the config for its key:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@task\ndef research_task(self) -&gt; Task:\n    return Task(config=self.tasks_config[&quot;research_task&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0129","card":"q-crewai-029-crew-py-complete","sec":"crewai-s028","q":"Which task adds <code>output_file</code> in <code>crew.py</code>, and how?","a":"<p><code>formatting_task</code> writes the article to a Markdown file:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@task\ndef formatting_task(self) -&gt; Task:\n    return Task(\n        config=self.tasks_config[&quot;formatting_task&quot;],\n        output_file=&quot;technical_article.md&quot;\n    )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0130","card":"q-crewai-029-crew-py-complete","sec":"crewai-s028","q":"How does <code>@crew</code> assemble the crew without a manual list?","a":"<p><code>self.agents</code> and <code>self.tasks</code> auto-collect every <code>@agent</code> and <code>@task</code> method:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@crew\ndef crew(self) -&gt; Crew:\n    return Crew(\n        agents=self.agents,\n        tasks=self.tasks,\n        process=Process.sequential,\n        verbose=True\n    )</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0131","card":"q-crewai-030-main-py-and-running","sec":"crewai-s029","q":"What does <code>main.py</code> contain and how is each function run?","a":"<p>Four functions, each runnable through the CLI:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>CLI</th><th>Function</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>crewai run</code></td><td><code>run()</code></td><td>Run the full workflow</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>crewai train</code></td><td><code>train()</code></td><td>Train with feedback to improve outputs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>crewai replay</code></td><td><code>replay()</code></td><td>Jump to a specific task and replay from there</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>crewai test</code></td><td><code>test()</code></td><td>Run N iterations with performance metrics</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0132","card":"q-crewai-030-main-py-and-running","sec":"crewai-s029","q":"How does <code>run()</code> in <code>main.py</code> start the technical writing crew?","a":"<p>It builds inputs with the topic and calls <code>kickoff</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def run():\n    inputs = {\n        &quot;topic&quot;: &quot;Introduction to GraphQL&quot;\n    }\n    try:\n        TechnicalWritingCrew().crew().kickoff(inputs=inputs)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0133","card":"q-crewai-030-main-py-and-running","sec":"crewai-s029","q":"What do <code>TechnicalWritingCrew()</code>, <code>.crew()</code> and <code>.kickoff(inputs=)</code> each do?","a":"<p><code>TechnicalWritingCrew()</code> creates the class. <code>.crew()</code> returns the <code>Crew</code>. <code>.kickoff(inputs=)</code> starts the workflow.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0134","card":"q-crewai-030-main-py-and-running","sec":"crewai-s029","q":"How do you run the technical writing crew?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>crewai run</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0135","card":"q-crewai-030-main-py-and-running","sec":"crewai-s029","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, what is the flow of the technical writing run?","a":"<p>Researcher (web search, notes), strategist (outline), writer (full draft, the longest step), editor (review), editor (format), then <code>technical_article.md</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0136","card":"q-crewai-030-main-py-and-running","sec":"crewai-s029","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, which sections did the GraphQL article have?","a":"<p>Introduction, What is GraphQL, Key Principles (type system, single graph, query hierarchy), Code Examples, Use Cases, Best Practices, Security Considerations, Challenges, Transitioning from REST to GraphQL, Conclusion and References.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"crewai-f0137","card":"q-crewai-030-main-py-and-running","sec":"crewai-s029","q":"In the CrewAI technical writing crew, what code example appeared in the GraphQL article?","a":"<p>A query for a user by id:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query {\n  user(id: &quot;1&quot;) {\n    name\n    email\n  }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true}];
